class QgsDropUtils
{
%Docstring(signature="appended")
Inspects the mime data of a drag which brings map data into QGIS.

Any consuming widget (main window, layer tree, map canvas) or any custom
drop handlers all gets the infos it needs from this helper.

.. versionadded:: 4.4
%End

%TypeHeaderCode
#include "qgsdroputils.h"
%End
  public:
    static bool isDatasetDrag( const QMimeData *data );
%Docstring
Returns ``True`` if ``data`` is a drag of datasets into QGIS: local
files, or uris coming from within QGIS itself such as browser panel
entries.

Widgets which accept these alongside drags of their own contents, as the
layer tree does when its nodes are reordered, use this to tell the two
apart.
%End

    static QStringList files( const QMimeData *data );
%Docstring
Returns the local files carried by ``data``, in the order they were
dragged.
%End

    static bool hasCustomUri( const QMimeData *data, const QString &providerKey );
%Docstring
Returns ``True`` if ``data`` carries a custom uri whose provider key is
``providerKey``, that is, one
:py:func:`QgsCustomDropHandler.handleCustomUriDrop()` would be called
with.

This is a convenience for a :py:class:`QgsCustomDropHandler` which
accepts the browser entries it created.
%End

    static bool hasFileExtension( const QMimeData *data, const QStringList &extensions );
%Docstring
Returns ``True`` if ``data`` carries a local file whose complete suffix
is one of ``extensions``, given without a leading dot and matched case
insensitively.

This is a convenience for a :py:class:`QgsCustomDropHandler` which
accepts a fixed set of file types.
%End
};

